Local correction (not an upstream backport): discovered macOS font files are
indexed on at most two scoped workers, then aggregated in the original order.
All worker lifetimes join before the resulting collection is used. No font
paths, aliases, face metadata or fallback policy are removed. Thread creation
failure uses the original synchronous scanning for that chunk. Other platform
discovery is unchanged. Tests compare complete system metadata with the retained
serial implementation, including aliases, PostScript names and faces.
The distribution Cargo.lock is omitted; the application retains its pinned lock.
UPSTREAM.json records the exact original archive/file hashes and local changes.
Fresh native startup/resource and full three-target quality gates are required.
